---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import BreadCrumb from "@/components/breadcrumb/BreadCrumb";
import { brand } from "@/config/brand";
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${brand.name}`}
  description={`Privacy Policy for ${brand.legalName}. Learn how we handle project data, communication details, and respect your privacy.`}
>
  <BreadCrumb client:load title="Privacy Policy" />
  
  <section class="tz-pt-60 tz-pb-60 tz-pt-lg-120 tz-pb-lg-120 tz-bg-neutral3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
          <div class="p-4 p-lg-5 rounded-3 tz-bg-neutral2 border border-secondary text-white">
            <h2 class="tz-display-4 mb-4 text-uppercase tz-text-neutral5">Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-m mb-4">
              <strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 2026
            </p>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">1. Overview</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              {brand.legalName} ("Vesharo", "we", "us", or "our") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting any personal and business information you share with us through our website ({brand.seo.siteUrl}) and direct consulting communications.
            </p>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">2. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              We collect information that you voluntarily provide to us when requesting proposals, booking technical consultations, or subscribing to engineering insights:
            </p>
            <ul class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light ps-4 mb-3">
              <li>Contact details (Name, business email address, company name)</li>
              <li>Project scope, technical specifications, and budget preferences</li>
              <li>Standard website analytics (browser type, anonymized IP, pages visited) to ensure site reliability</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              We use collected information solely for legitimate business operations:
            </p>
            <ul class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light ps-4 mb-3">
              <li>Evaluating and responding to your project inquiries and RFP submissions</li>
              <li>Delivering agreed-upon software engineering and IT consulting services</li>
              <li>Sending requested technical newsletters and company updates (with one-click unsubscribe)</li>
              <li>Maintaining system security and preventing unauthorized access</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">4. Intellectual Property &amp; NDA Protection</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              All proprietary project requirements, codebases, and architectural discussions shared with Vesharo are treated as strictly confidential. We execute standard mutual Non-Disclosure Agreements (NDAs) prior to detailed discovery and scoping sessions upon request.
            </p>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">5. Data Sharing &amp; Third Parties</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal or project data to any third parties. Data is processed only through secure, enterprise-grade cloud providers (such as AWS, Google Cloud, and encrypted email infrastructure) required to operate our services.
            </p>

            <h3 class="tz-text-neutral5 mt-4 mb-3">6. Contact Us</h3>
            <p class="tz-text-neutral6 tz-text-l fw-light">
              If you have any questions regarding this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise data rights, please contact our data privacy team at:
              <br />
              <a href={`mailto:${brand.contact.email}`} class="tz-text-primary fw-medium">{brand.contact.email}</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
